markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Utilizing the Capstone Project Handout & Digital Levels 

The Capstone Project Handout acts as a roadmap and checklist for the project, helping students track their milestone deliverables and daily progress.

However, the actual thinking, reasoning, and decision-making are captured digitally as the project evolves across different "levels" on the computer platform
.
While the Handout tracks where they are in the project, the final app shows what was built.

Most importantly, the students' digital `capstone.md` file and their Benchmark Reflections explain the how and why.

---

<div style="display:flex; gap:32px; align-items:flex-start; flex-wrap:wrap; font-family:'Geist', Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">

  <!-- Left Column -->
<div style="flex:1 1 250px; min-width:250px;">
    <h3>What It Covers</h3>

  <p>
      The digital levels mirror the project's milestones and provide designated spaces for students to track their progress:
    </p>

   <ul>
      <li><strong>Intent &amp; Scope</strong> (Day 1): Level 1</li>
      <li><strong>System Explanation</strong> (Day 2): Level 2</li>
      <li><strong>Testing &amp; Behavior</strong> (Day 3+): Level 4</li>
      <li><strong>Feedback &amp; Iteration</strong> (Day 8): Level 6</li>
      <li><strong>Final Reflection</strong>: Levels 8, 9, and 10 </li>
     <li><i>Note: Scheduled Benchmark Reflections occur on Levels 3, 5, and 7</i></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- Right Column -->
  <div style="flex:2.3 1 500px; min-width:320px;">

  <div style="background:#fff; border-radius:10px; box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.08); padding:24px; font-family:'Geist', Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#222; line-height:1.5;">

   <h2 style="margin:0 0 10px 0; color:#4C42CF; font-size:30px; font-weight:700;">
        Milestones &amp; Deliverables
      </h2>

  <p style="margin:0 0 24px 0; font-size:12pt;">
        Use this checklist to track your progress across the capstone. You may work across milestones on the same day. Return to earlier milestones anytime your idea, scope, or system design changes.
      </p>

  <h3 style="margin:0 0 10px 0; color:#2191CC; font-size:22px; font-weight:700;">
        Milestone 1: Intent &amp; Scope
      </h3>

  <p style="margin:0 0 18px 0; font-size:12pt;">
        <strong>Goal:</strong> We can clearly explain who this is for, what problem it solves, and what this version will include.
      </p>

  <fieldset style="border:none; padding:0; margin:0 0 20px 0;">
        <legend style="position:absolute; left:-9999px;">
          Milestone 1 checklist
        </legend>

  <div style="margin-bottom:12px;">
          <input type="checkbox" id="item1" style="margin-right:10px; transform:scale(1.15);">
          <label for="item1" style="font-size:12pt;">
            We can describe our app's audience and the problem it addresses
          </label>
        </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom:12px;">
          <input type="checkbox" id="item2" style="margin-right:10px; transform:scale(1.15);">
          <label for="item2" style="font-size:12pt;">
            We can explain what our first version will include and what we intentionally left out
          </label>
        </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom:12px;">
          <input type="checkbox" id="item3" style="margin-right:10px; transform:scale(1.15);">
          <label for="item3" style="font-size:12pt;">
            We can explain the tradeoffs we made to keep our scope realistic
          </label>
        </div>

  </fieldset>

  <p style="margin:0; font-size:12pt;">
        <strong>Levels to use:</strong> Level 1 - Milestone 1 choices
      </p>

  </div>

  </div>

</div>

---

## Using the Project Guide to Manage

<!-- Pacing & Redirection -->
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/a6383b704bd9c70435c6eb9c54f81352-image-1776699709862.png" alt="compass icon" style="width: 20%; max-width: 120px; height: auto; border-radius: 12px;">
  <div style="flex: 1; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);">
    <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Pacing &amp; Redirection</b></h3>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px;">If students are rushing to write code on Day 2, redirect them to <b>Level 2</b> to work on their System Explanation.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">Require them to clearly explain the flow of one user interaction (user action → app decision → user sees) before they are allowed to build.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Evidence for Grading -->
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/f8904ce9bbd20f037eb7b5b6f701cc15-image-1776699786662.png" alt="clipboard icon" style="width: 20%; max-width: 120px; height: auto; border-radius: 12px;">
  <div style="flex: 1; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);">
    <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Evidence for Grading</b></h3>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">The <code>capstone.md</code> file and the Benchmark Reflections on Levels 3, 5, and 7 are your primary artifacts for grading. You will use these digital records to assess the Project Planning & Intentional Design and Responsible AI & Ethical Reflection categories on the rubric.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Justifying Decisions -->
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/e03c589871538d69ec74607fa153fb6a-image-1776699823913.png" alt="magnifying glass icon" style="width: 20%; max-width: 120px; height: auto; border-radius: 12px;">
  <div style="flex: 1; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);">
    <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px;"><b>Justifying Decisions</b></h3>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px;">Remind students that their written reflections and chat logs on these levels are concrete evidence of their learning, not just busywork. Use their <code>capstone.md</code> logs to push teams to justify why they changed a feature based on a test or piece of feedback, rather than just listing what they changed
</p>
   
  </div>
</div>


MARKDOWN
